A||||21||extinct||Formula options||||1||
Z||000000||extinct||10-09-2001||02:06 AM||||What options could you get on the 88 formula:<P>Power trunk release ?<BR>Rear window defog?<BR>PW?<BR>PM?<BR>PW?<BR>Cruise control?<BR>Subwoofer?<P><BR>Were any of these standard on the Formula?<p>[This message has been edited by extinct (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierobear||10-09-2001||02:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by extinct:<BR><B>What options could you get on the 88 formula:<P>Power trunk release ? Don't think so<BR>Rear window defog? Yes (mine has one)<BR>PW?  yes<BR>PM?  no<BR>PW?<BR>Cruise control? yes<BR>Subwoofer?  no<P><BR>Were any of these standard on the Formula?<P>of the above, don't know what, if anything, was standard.<P>[This message has been edited by extinct (edited 10-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-09-2001||05:00 AM||||fierobear is correct....you could get most every option <B>except</B> power mirrors and a sub system (for whatever reason).<BR>As far as "standard"..hard to say. I can tell you that on my Formula the only options its got is a sunroof, air, automatic transmission, and am/fm cassette...thats it. NO power windows, NO power locks, NO rear defrost (who needs that on a Fiero anyway?)and NO power trunk release. Its a plain-jainer...........<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||10-09-2001||07:32 AM||||According to Mark Corbin's 'Fiero Spotter's Guide', Lumbar Seats and a 4-cyl Engine were the only items specifically denied to Formulas. Lumbar Seats were GT-only, and 4-cyls were Coupe-only.<P>279 Formulas came with Power Decklid Release;<BR>94 Formulas came with Power Mirrors; and<BR>8 Formulas came with a factory-installed Subwoofer-equipped stereo system.<P>*Everybody* on this list should have one of these booklets... they're incredible.<P>Copies are available for $4.00 plus $1.00 Shipping and Handling from:<P>FIERO SPOTTER'S GUIDE<BR>5474 S.R. 19<BR>Galion, OH 44833<P>Make checks payable to Mark Corbin.<P>------------------<P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||10-09-2001||09:21 AM||||My formula has auto, am/fm, rear window defog.  it had cruise and ac, and it will have a sunroof and ground effects.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||10-09-2001||09:31 AM||||Formulas came equipped with power brakes, a V-6, the GT suspension and wheels, and a wing. Bare bones. Everything else was optional.<P>Don't think leather was available, either.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||10-09-2001||11:35 AM||||I've been told that No formula's ever came from the factory with power trunk release. <P>Some dealers installed it as it could be got in kit form and installed in 10 min. <BR>1. Just plug in the switch and relay inside.<BR>2. Bolt the solenoid to the latch.<BR>3. Pull the old wire harness out of the decklid and push the new one in.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||10-09-2001||11:42 AM||||If I am not mistaken, the information in the Fiero Spotter's Guide was taken from the factory build code listings, so the numbers I mentioned reflect options installed at the factory, not by the dealership.<P>It would be a vastly more difficult task to compile information about specific dealer-installed options collected from every Pontiac dealship across the globe than it would to obtain the master lists of the factory-built codes from the single manufacturing plant where they were made.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88CoupeV6||10-09-2001||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>If I am not mistaken, the information in the Fiero Spotter's Guide was taken from the factory build code listings,</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Opps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I didn't even see your post. Sorry <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just skipped down to post. I just heard my info online somewhere maybe here and thought I would state what I had heard. <P>||||reg||7
Z||000009||extinct||10-10-2001||12:37 AM||||Thanks for the reply(s)!  So what would one need if you wanted to add power trunk release on  forumula that did not come with it.<P>Thanks again...||||reg||1
Z||000010||88CoupeV6||10-10-2001||10:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by extinct:<BR><B>Thanks for the reply(s)!  So what would one need if you wanted to add power trunk release on  forumula that did not come with it.<P>Thanks again...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You would need <BR>1. the dash switch, <BR>2. the relay that plugs in under the dash below the switch area into the 3 prong connector.<BR>3. the decklid wires off a car with the release. The wires feed themselves up the decklid when  you thread them in. you only have a 3 wire one now. the new one will have 4 wires and plugs into the connector.<BR>4. the solenoid that has one bolt and goes on the latch. The rest of the car is all wired for it.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000011||extinct||10-11-2001||07:25 PM||||Thanks Mr. UPS man.. I may have further questions for you later.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||08:51 AM||||WHAT!!!! ??? Only 94 with power mirrors?? Any RPO code to look for that? My white Formula has power locks and power mirrors. I need to know if it is original and thus that unique  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I remember whe I ordered my 1st Formula that thay didn't offered the sub option and neither the leather. But I do remember there was an options package that included the cruise, PL & PM. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||NIFE [PaulV]||10-12-2001||09:42 AM||||The dealer order guides show that for the Formula, there were no options to order PM, Sub woofer, leather, rear power latch or lumbar seats. (or luggage carrier, since the wing was standard equipment). PW, PDL, etc were available.<BR>The ISA, ISB, and ISC packages available on the order guide for the 88 coupe and Formula did not include PM's.<BR>The ISA package for the GT did include PM's.<BR>If a Formula has PM's , most likely they were put on later, but anything could have happened as production ground down!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||11:40 AM||||Is the wiring for PM embeded in all Fieros? If yes then maybe I can check that to see if they came from the factory. Any detail in particular that I can check for that? In the installation? I'm really interested to see if this one was one of those 94. I bought it from someone that I doubt took all the hassle to install that later. TIA||||reg||1
Z||000015||LZeitgeist||10-12-2001||02:32 PM||||It's really simple... check the decal on top of the driver's side front fender inside the front storage compartment and match up the codes there with the list in the Fiero Spotter's Guide. That will tell you exactly what options were built into the car at the factory. <P>Best five bucks you'll ever spend as a Fiero owner. (And no, I gain nothing from this free advertising... I am just one of many very happy customers.)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||03:17 PM||||Ok, so there is one code specific for PM or one group code like the 'ISA' code NIFE mentioned? If one code exist, anyone can tell me which it is? I can spend the $5 later to show people how rare it is. Tks||||reg||5
Z||000017||Phil||10-12-2001||03:52 PM||||If the car did not come with PM the wiring is not there.||||reg||1
